window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["apache-spark"]=[{"id":"apache-spark-f0001","card":"q-apache-spark-001-1-data-engineering-concepts","sec":"apache-spark-s001","q":"What is data engineering?","a":"<p>Designing and building systems that collect, move, process and store data at scale and low latency, so analytics and ML can use it. Roles: Data Engineer, Big Data Architect.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0002","card":"q-apache-spark-001-1-data-engineering-concepts","sec":"apache-spark-s001","q":"Why is data engineering a prerequisite for ML?","a":"<p>Training data must be cleansed and transformed, and inference also needs pre-processing and post-processing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0003","card":"q-apache-spark-002-data-engineering-vs-analytics-vs-data-sc","sec":"apache-spark-s002","q":"Data engineering vs business analytics vs data science: what does each cover?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Scope</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Data Engineering</td><td>Integrating source systems, building pipelines, transport and processing, transforming/aggregating, storing. Prepares data.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Business Analytics</td><td>Works on prepared data: dashboards, reports, exploratory analytics, statistical modeling, recommendations.</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Data Science</td><td>Encompasses both, plus machine learning and predictions.</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0004","card":"q-apache-spark-003-the-five-data-engineering-functions","sec":"apache-spark-s003","q":"What are the five data engineering functions?","a":"<p>Acquisition, Transport, Storage, Processing and Serving.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0005","card":"q-apache-spark-003-the-five-data-engineering-functions","sec":"apache-spark-s003","q":"What is the goal of Acquisition in data engineering, and what are its key considerations?","a":"<p>The goal is to extract or receive data from the source. Considerations: source format conversion, extract vs expose interface, security, reliability, latency.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0006","card":"q-apache-spark-003-the-five-data-engineering-functions","sec":"apache-spark-s003","q":"What is the goal of Transport in data engineering, and what are its key considerations?","a":"<p>The goal is to move data to processing or storage endpoints. Considerations: reliability, integrity, scale, security/privacy, latency, cost.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0007","card":"q-apache-spark-003-the-five-data-engineering-functions","sec":"apache-spark-s003","q":"What is the goal of Storage in data engineering, and what are its key considerations?","a":"<p>The goal is to store data for downstream use. Considerations: schema flexibility, popular query patterns, availability, redundancy, cost.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0008","card":"q-apache-spark-003-the-five-data-engineering-functions","sec":"apache-spark-s003","q":"What is the goal of Processing in data engineering, and what are its key considerations?","a":"<p>The goal is to transform and enrich data. Considerations: scale, resiliency, latency, security, cleansing/filtering/enriching, aggregation, real-time ML predictions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0009","card":"q-apache-spark-003-the-five-data-engineering-functions","sec":"apache-spark-s003","q":"What is the goal of Serving in data engineering, and what are its key considerations?","a":"<p>The goal is to expose data to consumers. Considerations: APIs or push to endpoints, latency, availability, security, consumer skill levels, flexible schema.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0010","card":"q-apache-spark-004-batch-vs-real-time-stream-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s004","q":"Batch vs real-time processing: how do the input and input changes differ?","a":"<p>Batch input is a complete bounded batch (by record count or date/time range) and does not change during processing. Real-time input is unbounded: records arrive as created, one at a time, and may change during processing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0011","card":"q-apache-spark-004-batch-vs-real-time-stream-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s004","q":"Batch vs real-time processing: how do latency and results differ?","a":"<p>Batch has higher latency because it waits for the batch, and gives results at the end (intermediate possible). Real-time has low latency (seconds) and gives continuous results.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0012","card":"q-apache-spark-004-batch-vs-real-time-stream-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s004","q":"Batch vs real-time processing: how do complexity, reprocessing and state differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>Batch</th><th>Real-time</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Complexity</td><td>Simpler</td><td>More complex (state management, change data capture)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reprocessing</td><td>Same input gives same output</td><td>Must account for changes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>State</td><td>Generally stateless</td><td>State management critical (entity states, running summaries)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0013","card":"q-apache-spark-004-batch-vs-real-time-stream-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s004","q":"How do you choose between batch and real-time processing?","a":"<p>Not every use case needs real-time. Choose on latency requirement versus complexity.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0014","card":"q-apache-spark-005-why-spark-for-data-engineering","sec":"apache-spark-s005","q":"Why use Spark for data engineering?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Handles both batch and real-time.</li>\n  <li>Native support for RDBMS, Kafka, HDFS.</li>\n  <li>Parallel processing for large-scale real-time data.</li>\n  <li>MapReduce, windowing, state management, joins.</li>\n  <li>Graph processing and ML can be integrated into pipelines.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0015","card":"q-apache-spark-006-architecture-and-execution-flow","sec":"apache-spark-s006","q":"What do the driver node and executor nodes do in Spark?","a":"<p>The driver node runs the Spark program. Executor nodes in the cluster do the work in parallel.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0016","card":"q-apache-spark-006-architecture-and-execution-flow","sec":"apache-spark-s006","q":"What is the Spark execution flow from source to destination?","a":"<p>Read the source, convert to DataFrame/RDD (partitioned across executors), transform (map/filter, local on each executor, no data movement), action (reduce/group by, shuffle between executors), collect (partitions merged to the driver), write to the destination.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0017","card":"q-apache-spark-006-architecture-and-execution-flow","sec":"apache-spark-s006","q":"In Spark, how do transforms, actions and collect compare in data movement and bottleneck risk?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Data movement</th><th>Bottleneck risk</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Transforms (map, filter)</td><td>None, local on partitions</td><td>Low, fully parallel</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Actions (reduce, group by)</td><td>Shuffle between executors</td><td>High (I/O and memory)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Collect</td><td>Partitions merged to driver</td><td>Moderate</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0018","card":"q-apache-spark-006-architecture-and-execution-flow","sec":"apache-spark-s006","q":"How do you find bottlenecks in a Spark pipeline?","a":"<p>Visualize the execution flow for each pipeline.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0019","card":"q-apache-spark-007-parallel-reads-processing-writes","sec":"apache-spark-s007","q":"How does Spark read in parallel from JDBC and from Kafka?","a":"<p>JDBC: partition by column values, and each executor reads a subset. Kafka: each executor reads a subset of Kafka partitions.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0020","card":"q-apache-spark-007-parallel-reads-processing-writes","sec":"apache-spark-s007","q":"How does Spark write in parallel to JDBC and to Kafka?","a":"<p>JDBC: each executor writes in parallel (configurable), and writes can be batched to cut network I/O. Kafka: executors write to topics in parallel.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0021","card":"q-apache-spark-007-parallel-reads-processing-writes","sec":"apache-spark-s007","q":"What is predicate pushdown in Spark?","a":"<p>Filters are pushed to the data source so unwanted records are never read into memory. The optimizer does it automatically.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0022","card":"q-apache-spark-007-parallel-reads-processing-writes","sec":"apache-spark-s007","q":"Which Spark operations are parallel, and which introduce shuffling?","a":"<p>Map and filter are parallel. Reduce introduces shuffling.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0023","card":"q-apache-spark-007-parallel-reads-processing-writes","sec":"apache-spark-s007","q":"What are the rules of thumb for speeding up a Spark pipeline?","a":"<p>Do map-type work and filtering early, reduce shuffling by using the right partitions, and repartition as needed. Pipeline speed is set by its slowest bottleneck.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0024","card":"q-apache-spark-008-execution-plan-lazy-evaluation","sec":"apache-spark-s008","q":"What is lazy evaluation in Spark?","a":"<p>Spark runs code only when an action (reduce, collect) is called. It then analyzes all prior steps and builds an optimized physical plan.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0025","card":"q-apache-spark-008-execution-plan-lazy-evaluation","sec":"apache-spark-s008","q":"What does the Spark optimizer do?","a":"<p>It reduces I/O, shuffling and memory use, reads in parallel from executors (not the driver) where the source allows, and applies predicate pushdown.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0026","card":"q-apache-spark-008-execution-plan-lazy-evaluation","sec":"apache-spark-s008","q":"How do you find optimizations in a Spark job?","a":"<p>Print and analyze execution plans.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0027","card":"q-apache-spark-009-stateful-stream-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s009","q":"What is checkpointing in Spark streaming and what does it save?","a":"<p>It saves pipeline state to persistent storage (HDFS, S3) so a failed job resumes where it left off. It saves metadata (configuration, progress), Kafka offsets, key-based state, and RDDs for operations spanning batches (windowing).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0028","card":"q-apache-spark-009-stateful-stream-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s009","q":"What are watermarks in Spark streaming?","a":"<p>They are used for event-time windowing, where event time is when the event was created at the source, not when it arrived. A window must wait for all its events. The watermark is the delay to wait before processing a window. Spark tracks events until the watermark passes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0029","card":"q-apache-spark-009-stateful-stream-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s009","q":"What does <code>UpdateStateByKey</code> do in Spark streaming?","a":"<p>It tracks entity state by key (for example, a browser session ID). New events change state, and updated states are published as a DStream to downstream transformations.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0030","card":"q-apache-spark-010-spark-sql-and-ml","sec":"apache-spark-s010","q":"What is Spark SQL?","a":"<p>Standard-SQL syntax that is translated to distributed operations. It works on batch and streaming, can sit in the same pipeline, cascade (one output feeds the next), and persist to databases or streams.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0031","card":"q-apache-spark-010-spark-sql-and-ml","sec":"apache-spark-s010","q":"What does Spark ML provide?","a":"<p>Pre-processing (feature extraction, transformation, dimensionality reduction), popular algorithms, and ML pipelines that chain extraction, pre-processing, training and inference inside the same Spark pipeline.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0032","card":"q-apache-spark-010-spark-sql-and-ml","sec":"apache-spark-s010","q":"What does Spark offer as a platform for data work?","a":"<p>One integrated platform for data engineering, analytics and ML.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0033","card":"q-apache-spark-011-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What are the prerequisites and the stack for the Spark data engineering course environment?","a":"<p>Prerequisites: Spark basics, Structured Streaming, Spark SQL, Python/Jupyter, familiarity with Kafka, MariaDB, Redis and Docker. Stack: PySpark (built-in local Spark, no cluster needed), Docker (MariaDB, Kafka, Redis containers), Java 17, Anaconda, Jupyter.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0034","card":"q-apache-spark-011-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"How do you start the Spark course containers and check them?","a":"<p>Run docker-compose with <code>spark-docker.yml</code> from the exercise files, then verify that 3 containers are running.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>docker-compose -f spark-docker.yml up -d\ndocker ps  # Verify 3 containers running</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0035","card":"q-apache-spark-011-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What MariaDB setup does the course docker-compose file use?","a":"<p>Image <code>mariadb:11.4.2</code>, container <code>mariadb</code>, with these settings and port 3306.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>      - MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=spark\n      - MYSQL_USER=spark\n      - MYSQL_PASSWORD=spark\n      - MYSQL_DATABASE=spark_de\n      - &#x27;3306:3306&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0036","card":"q-apache-spark-011-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What Kafka setup does the course docker-compose file use?","a":"<p>Image <code>bitnami/kafka:3.6</code>, container <code>kafka-broker</code>, in KRaft mode (broker and controller in one node), exposed on port 9092.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>      - KAFKA_ENABLE_KRAFT=yes\n      - KAFKA_CFG_PROCESS_ROLES=broker,controller\n      - KAFKA_CFG_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=CLIENT://kafka:29092,EXTERNAL://localhost:9092\n      - &#x27;9092:9092&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0037","card":"q-apache-spark-011-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What Redis setup does the course docker-compose file use?","a":"<p>Image <code>redis:7.2.5-alpine</code>, container <code>redis</code>, port 6379.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    image: redis:7.2.5-alpine\n      - &#x27;6379:6379&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0038","card":"q-apache-spark-012-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"Which commands set up the MariaDB connector and conda environment for the Spark course on Mac?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>brew install mariadb-connector-c\nconda create -n spark python=3.11\nconda activate spark\njupyter notebook</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0039","card":"q-apache-spark-012-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"Which checks confirm the Java and PySpark environment variables in the Spark course?","a":"<p><code>JAVA_HOME</code> must point to the Java 17 folder and <code>PYSPARK_PYTHON</code> must point to \"python\".</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>java -version          # Verify Java 17\necho $JAVA_HOME        # Must point to Java 17 folder\necho $PYSPARK_PYTHON   # Must point to &quot;python&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0040","card":"q-apache-spark-012-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"Which Python packages and versions does the Spark course setup notebook install?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>!pip install pyspark==3.5.1\n!pip install findspark==2.0.1\n!pip install pandas==2.2.2\n!pip install mariadb==1.1.10\n!pip install kafka-python==2.0.2\n!pip install redis==5.0.7</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0041","card":"q-apache-spark-012-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"Which environment variable does the setup notebook set before installing PySpark?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>os.environ[&quot;PYSPARK_HADOOP_VERSION&quot;] = &quot;3&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0042","card":"q-apache-spark-012-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What extra steps does Windows need for the Spark course setup?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>Copy the hadoop folder to <code>c:\\hadoop</code>.</li>\n  <li>Set <code>HADOOP_HOME=c:\\hadoop</code>.</li>\n  <li>Add <code>c:\\hadoop\\bin</code> to PATH.</li>\n  <li>Restart the notebook.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0043","card":"q-apache-spark-012-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What three databases does the Spark course notebook create, and what pattern does it use?","a":"<p><code>warehouse_stock</code>, <code>global_stock</code> and <code>website_stats</code>. It repeats the same check-then-create pattern for each: list the databases, and create the database and table only if missing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0044","card":"q-apache-spark-012-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"How does the setup notebook connect as root and check whether a database exists in MariaDB?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>root_conn = mariadb.connect(\n    user=&quot;root&quot;, password=&quot;spark&quot;,\n    host=&quot;127.0.0.1&quot;, port=3306, database=&quot;mysql&quot;\n)\ndb_cursor = root_conn.cursor()\ndb_cursor.execute(&quot;SHOW DATABASES&quot;)\ndb_list = [database[0] for database in db_cursor.fetchall()]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0045","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What statements give the <code>spark</code> user access to a new database in the setup notebook?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db_cursor.execute(&quot;GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON warehouse_stock.* to &#x27;spark&#x27;@&#x27;%&#x27;&quot;)\ndb_cursor.execute(&quot;FLUSH PRIVILEGES&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0046","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What columns does the <code>warehouse_stock.item_stock</code> table have?","a":"<p><code>ID</code> (auto-increment primary key), <code>STOCK_DATE</code>, <code>WAREHOUSE_ID</code>, <code>ITEM_NAME</code>, <code>OPENING_STOCK</code>, <code>RECEIPTS</code>, <code>ISSUES</code> and <code>UNIT_VALUE</code>. It has an index on <code>STOCK_DATE</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0047","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What columns does the <code>global_stock.item_stock</code> table have?","a":"<p><code>ID</code> (auto-increment primary key), <code>STOCK_DATE</code>, <code>ITEM_NAME</code>, <code>TOTAL_REC</code>, <code>OPENING_STOCK</code>, <code>RECEIPTS</code>, <code>ISSUES</code>, <code>CLOSING_STOCK</code> and <code>CLOSING_VALUE</code>. It has an index on <code>STOCK_DATE</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0048","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What columns does the <code>website_stats.visit_stats</code> table have?","a":"<p><code>ID</code> (auto-increment primary key), <code>INTERVAL_TIMESTAMP</code>, <code>LAST_ACTION</code> and <code>DURATION</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0049","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"How does the setup notebook check that the tables were created?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>db_cursor.execute(&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    SELECT TABLE_SCHEMA, TABLE_NAME\n    FROM information_schema.tables\n    WHERE table_schema IN (&#x27;warehouse_stock&#x27;,&#x27;global_stock&#x27;,&#x27;website_stats&#x27;)\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0050","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"Which Kafka topics does the Spark course setup create?","a":"<p><code>spark.streaming.website.visits</code>, <code>spark.streaming.carts.abandoned</code> and <code>spark.exercise.lastaction.long</code>, each with 1 partition and replication factor 1.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0051","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"How does the setup notebook create Kafka topics with <code>kafka-python</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>admin_client = KafkaAdminClient(\n                bootstrap_servers=&quot;localhost:9092&quot;,\n                client_id=&#x27;spark-de&#x27;)\ntopic_list = [\n    NewTopic(name=&quot;spark.streaming.website.visits&quot;,\n             num_partitions=1, replication_factor=1),\n]\nresult = admin_client.create_topics(new_topics=topic_list, validate_only=False)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0052","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"How do you create the raw data folder and check Java in the Spark course setup?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>os.makedirs(&quot;./raw_data&quot;, exist_ok=True)\nprint(os.environ[&quot;JAVA_HOME&quot;])   # must point to Java 17</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0053","card":"q-apache-spark-013-3-environment-setup","sec":"apache-spark-s011","q":"What happens to databases and topics if the Spark course Docker containers are shut down?","a":"<p>They are lost. Rerun the setup notebook to recreate them.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0054","card":"q-apache-spark-014-4-batch-pipeline-warehouse-stock-aggrega","sec":"apache-spark-s012","q":"What is the use case of the Spark batch pipeline?","a":"<p>An enterprise has warehouses worldwide, each with its own stock app and local MariaDB (<code>warehouse_stock.item_stock</code>: opening stock, receipts, issues per item per day). The goal is a consolidated central stock database, collected daily, scalable to hundreds of warehouses.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0055","card":"q-apache-spark-014-4-batch-pipeline-warehouse-stock-aggrega","sec":"apache-spark-s012","q":"What is the architecture of the Spark warehouse stock batch pipeline?","a":"<p>Each warehouse runs a Stock Upload Job daily on its local Spark cluster. It reads the local MariaDB and writes Parquet to the central file system (HDFS/S3; local <code>raw_data/</code> is the proxy). After uploads complete, the Stock Aggregator Job on the central Spark cluster reads all Parquet, aggregates with Spark SQL, and writes to the <code>global_stock</code> MariaDB.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0056","card":"q-apache-spark-014-4-batch-pipeline-warehouse-stock-aggrega","sec":"apache-spark-s012","q":"Why does the Spark batch pipeline use Parquet, and how is the folder partitioned?","a":"<p>Parquet is columnar and efficient for parallel reads. The folder structure is partitioned by <code>STOCK_DATE</code> then <code>WAREHOUSE_ID</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0057","card":"q-apache-spark-014-4-batch-pipeline-warehouse-stock-aggrega","sec":"apache-spark-s012","q":"What are the four stages of the Spark warehouse stock pipeline flow?","a":"<p>Acquire (local MariaDB), Transport (Parquet to central FS), Consolidate (Spark SQL GROUP BY), Persist (global MariaDB). Prune <code>raw_data/</code> after processing.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0058","card":"q-apache-spark-015-4-1-local-db-connection-and-sample-data","sec":"apache-spark-s013","q":"How does the batch notebook connect to the local warehouse MariaDB and reset its data?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>local_db_conn = mariadb.connect(\n    user=&quot;spark&quot;,\n    password=&quot;spark&quot;,\n    host=&quot;127.0.0.1&quot;,\n    port=3306,\n    database=&quot;warehouse_stock&quot;,\n    autocommit=True\n)\nlocal_cursor = local_db_conn.cursor()\n# Delete existing data if needed (reinitialize)\nlocal_cursor.execute(&quot;DELETE FROM warehouse_stock.item_stock&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0059","card":"q-apache-spark-015-4-1-local-db-connection-and-sample-data","sec":"apache-spark-s013","q":"How does <code>generate_data</code> create random stock values for each item?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>opening_stock = random.randint(1,100)\nreceipts=random.randint(1,50)\nissues=random.randint(1, opening_stock+receipts)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0060","card":"q-apache-spark-015-4-1-local-db-connection-and-sample-data","sec":"apache-spark-s013","q":"Which sample data does the batch notebook create for the warehouses?","a":"<p>Stock rows for the last 3 dates, for the warehouses NewYork, LosAngeles and London.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>generate_data(generate_dates,&quot;NewYork&quot;)\ngenerate_data(generate_dates,&quot;LosAngeles&quot;)\ngenerate_data(generate_dates,&quot;London&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0061","card":"q-apache-spark-015-4-1-local-db-connection-and-sample-data","sec":"apache-spark-s013","q":"How does the batch notebook count records per warehouse?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>local_cursor.execute(&quot;&quot;&quot;SELECT `WAREHOUSE_ID`, count(*) AS RECS\n                        FROM `warehouse_stock`.`item_stock`\n                        GROUP BY `WAREHOUSE_ID`&quot;&quot;&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0062","card":"q-apache-spark-016-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"How is the Spark session for the StockUploaderJob built?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>local_spark = SparkSession\\\n    .builder\\\n    .appName(&quot;StockUploaderJob&quot;)\\\n    .config(&quot;spark.sql.shuffle.partitions&quot;, 2)\\\n    .config(&quot;spark.default.parallelism&quot;, 2)\\\n    .master(&quot;local[2]&quot;)\\\n    .getOrCreate()\nlocal_spark.sparkContext.setLogLevel(&quot;WARN&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0063","card":"q-apache-spark-016-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"How do the batch notebook jobs add the MariaDB JDBC driver jar to Spark?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>.config(&quot;spark.jars&quot;, &quot;jars/mysql-connector-j-8.4.0.jar&quot;) \\\n.config(&quot;spark.driver.extraClassPath&quot;,&quot;jars/mysql-connector-j-8.4.0.jar&quot;) \\</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0064","card":"q-apache-spark-016-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"Why does <code>upload_stock</code> run a min/max <code>ID</code> query before the JDBC read?","a":"<p>The bounds feed the parallel JDBC read (<code>lowerBound</code> / <code>upperBound</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>SELECT min(`ID`) as MIN_ID, max(`ID`) as MAX_ID</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0065","card":"q-apache-spark-016-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"Why does the JDBC URL in the stock upload job say <code>mysql</code> instead of <code>mariadb</code>?","a":"<p>It is a workaround for a mariadb connector bug in Spark (SPARK-25013).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>.option(&quot;url&quot;, &quot;jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/warehouse_stock&quot;)\\</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0066","card":"q-apache-spark-017-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"How does Spark read the stock query from MariaDB in parallel?","a":"<p>Set <code>partitionColumn</code>, <code>lowerBound</code>, <code>upperBound</code> and <code>numPartitions</code> on the JDBC read.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    .option(&quot;partitionColumn&quot;,&quot;ID&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;lowerBound&quot;, min_bounds)\\\n    .option(&quot;upperBound&quot;,max_bounds + 1)\\\n    .option(&quot;numPartitions&quot;,2)\\\n    .load()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0067","card":"q-apache-spark-017-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"How does Spark write the stock DataFrame to the central store?","a":"<p>Append Parquet files, partitioned by date and warehouse.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>stock_df.write\\\n    .mode(&quot;append&quot;)\\\n    .partitionBy(&quot;STOCK_DATE&quot;,&quot;WAREHOUSE_ID&quot;)\\\n    .parquet(&quot;raw_data/&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0068","card":"q-apache-spark-017-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"What are the design decisions of the stock upload job and why?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Design decision</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>partitionColumn</code> + <code>lowerBound</code>/<code>upperBound</code> + <code>numPartitions</code></td><td>Parallel JDBC reads across executors. Bounds come from a min/max ID query first</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Query wrapped as subquery in <code>dbtable</code></td><td>Filter runs in the database (predicate pushdown)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>mysql</code> in the JDBC URL</td><td>Workaround for the mariadb connector bug in Spark</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>partitionBy(\"STOCK_DATE\",\"WAREHOUSE_ID\")</code></td><td>Subfolder structure for efficient filtered reads</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>raw_data/</code></td><td>Local proxy. Use an S3/HDFS URL in production</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0069","card":"q-apache-spark-017-4-2-upload-stock-to-the-central-store-pa","sec":"apache-spark-s014","q":"How do you wrap a query as a subquery in the JDBC <code>dbtable</code> option?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>.option(&quot;dbtable&quot;, &quot;( &quot; + stock_query + &quot; ) as tmpStock&quot;)\\</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0070","card":"q-apache-spark-018-4-3-aggregate-across-warehouses","sec":"apache-spark-s015","q":"How does the GlobalAggregatorJob read the uploaded Parquet and register it for SQL?","a":"<p>It reads all dates at once (it can read one date at a time by appending the date directory to the path) and creates a temp view.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>global_stock_df = global_spark.read.parquet(&quot;raw_data/&quot;)\nglobal_stock_df.createOrReplaceTempView(&quot;GLOBAL_STOCK&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0071","card":"q-apache-spark-018-4-3-aggregate-across-warehouses","sec":"apache-spark-s015","q":"Which Spark SQL query consolidates stock across warehouses?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_df = global_spark.sql(&quot;&quot;&quot;\n                    SELECT STOCK_DATE, ITEM_NAME,\n                            COUNT(*) as TOTAL_REC,\n                            SUM(OPENING_STOCK) as OPENING_STOCK,\n                            SUM(RECEIPTS) as RECEIPTS,\n                            SUM(ISSUES) as ISSUES,\n                            SUM( OPENING_STOCK + RECEIPTS - ISSUES) as CLOSING_STOCK,\n                            SUM( (OPENING_STOCK + RECEIPTS - ISSUES) * UNIT_VALUE ) as CLOSING_VALUE\n                            FROM GLOBAL_STOCK\n                            GROUP BY STOCK_DATE, ITEM_NAME\n                        &quot;&quot;&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0072","card":"q-apache-spark-018-4-3-aggregate-across-warehouses","sec":"apache-spark-s015","q":"How is closing stock and closing value calculated in the global aggregation?","a":"<p>Closing stock is the sum of <code>OPENING_STOCK + RECEIPTS - ISSUES</code>. Closing value is the sum of that times <code>UNIT_VALUE</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0073","card":"q-apache-spark-018-4-3-aggregate-across-warehouses","sec":"apache-spark-s015","q":"How does the aggregator write the summary to the <code>global_stock</code> MariaDB?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_df.write\\\n    .mode(&quot;append&quot;)\\\n    .format(&quot;jdbc&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;url&quot;, &quot;jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/global_stock&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;dbtable&quot;, &quot;global_stock.item_stock&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;user&quot;, &quot;spark&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;password&quot;, &quot;spark&quot;)\\\n    .save()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0074","card":"q-apache-spark-018-4-3-aggregate-across-warehouses","sec":"apache-spark-s015","q":"What happens to the <code>raw_data</code> files after the aggregator finishes?","a":"<p>Pruning: after processing is over, delete the files in <code>raw_data</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0075","card":"q-apache-spark-018-4-3-aggregate-across-warehouses","sec":"apache-spark-s015","q":"How do you verify the aggregate against the local databases in the batch pipeline?","a":"<p>Query one item and date (<code>Pencil Box</code> on <code>start_date</code>) in both the local <code>warehouse_stock</code> databases and the <code>global_stock</code> database, then compare the opening stock, receipts and issues.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>WHERE `ITEM_NAME` = &#x27;Pencil Box&#x27;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0076","card":"q-apache-spark-019-5-real-time-pipeline-website-analytics","sec":"apache-spark-s016","q":"What is the use case of the Spark real-time pipeline?","a":"<p>An e-commerce site tracks visits (date, country, duration, last action before exit: Catalog, FAQ, ShoppingCart, Order).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0077","card":"q-apache-spark-019-5-real-time-pipeline-website-analytics","sec":"apache-spark-s016","q":"What three real-time outputs does the website analytics pipeline need?","a":"<ol>\n  <li>5-second summaries of duration by last action go to MariaDB <code>website_stats.visit_stats</code>.</li>\n  <li>A running total of visit duration by country goes to a Redis sorted set.</li>\n  <li>Visits ending in ShoppingCart go to the Kafka topic <code>spark.streaming.carts.abandoned</code>.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0078","card":"q-apache-spark-019-5-real-time-pipeline-website-analytics","sec":"apache-spark-s016","q":"What is the architecture of the Spark website analytics pipeline, and what scales each part?","a":"<p>E-commerce app -&gt; Kafka <code>spark.streaming.website.visits</code> -&gt; one Spark job fanning out to MariaDB, Redis and the abandoned-carts Kafka topic. Kafka scales the source, Spark scales across executors, the Redis sorted set scales horizontally, and each executor writes to MariaDB in parallel.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0079","card":"q-apache-spark-020-5-1-generate-a-visits-stream-code-04-03","sec":"apache-spark-s017","q":"How do you create a Kafka producer for the visits topic with <code>kafka-python</code>?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>visits_producer = KafkaProducer(\n    bootstrap_servers=[&quot;localhost:9092&quot;],\n    key_serializer=string_serializer,\n    value_serializer=string_serializer\n)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0080","card":"q-apache-spark-020-5-1-generate-a-visits-stream-code-04-03","sec":"apache-spark-s017","q":"What does each fake visit record contain in the stream generator?","a":"<p>A <code>country</code>, <code>last_action</code>, <code>visit_date</code> and <code>duration</code> (1 to 20), sent as JSON.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>json_record[&quot;country&quot;] = countries[random.randint(0,4)]\njson_record[&quot;last_action&quot;] = last_actions[random.randint(0,3)]\njson_record[&quot;duration&quot;] = random.randint(1,20)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0081","card":"q-apache-spark-020-5-1-generate-a-visits-stream-code-04-03","sec":"apache-spark-s017","q":"Why does the visits producer use the country as the Kafka key?","a":"<p>Each country goes through the same partition, so updates for a country are handled sequentially.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>kafka_key = json_record[&quot;country&quot;]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0082","card":"q-apache-spark-020-5-1-generate-a-visits-stream-code-04-03","sec":"apache-spark-s017","q":"How does the visits producer send a record and pace the stream?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>visits_producer.send(visits_topic, key=kafka_key, value=kafka_value)\ntime.sleep(random.randint(1,3))   # sleep 1-3 seconds</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0083","card":"q-apache-spark-020-5-1-generate-a-visits-stream-code-04-03","sec":"apache-spark-s017","q":"How do you test that the visits topic data is published correctly?","a":"<p>Use a consumer cell that polls the topic and prints partition, offset and value.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>visits_consumer.subscribe(visits_topic)\nmessages = visits_consumer.poll()\nprint(&quot;Total messages :&quot;, len(messages))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0084","card":"q-apache-spark-021-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How does the Redis writer for the streaming job keep country totals?","a":"<p>It increments the country's duration in a sorted set with <code>zincrby</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>def write_to_redis(row):\n    stats_key = &quot;last-action-stats&quot;\n    redis_conn = redis.Redis(host=&quot;localhost&quot;, port=6379, decode_responses=True)\n    redis_conn.zincrby(stats_key, row[&quot;duration&quot;], row[&quot;country&quot;])\n    redis_conn.quit()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0085","card":"q-apache-spark-021-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How does the MariaDB writer store a 5-second summary row?","a":"<p>It inserts the window start, last action and duration into <code>visit_stats</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>INSERT INTO `website_stats`.`visit_stats`\n    (INTERVAL_TIMESTAMP, LAST_ACTION, DURATION)\nVALUES(&#x27;{row[&quot;window&quot;][&quot;start&quot;]}&#x27;,\n        &#x27;{row[&quot;last_action&quot;]}&#x27;,\n        &#x27;{row[&quot;duration&quot;]}&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0086","card":"q-apache-spark-021-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"What is the caveat of the <code>foreach</code> helper writers in the streaming job?","a":"<p>They open a connection per row. The notebook notes that production code should use a class instead (see the <code>DataStreamWriter.foreach</code> docs).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0087","card":"q-apache-spark-021-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"What schema does the streaming job use to parse visit records?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>schema = StructType([\n    StructField(&quot;country&quot;, StringType()),\n    StructField(&quot;last_action&quot;, StringType()),\n    StructField(&quot;visit_date&quot;, TimestampNTZType()),\n    StructField(&quot;duration&quot;, IntegerType())\n])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0088","card":"q-apache-spark-021-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"What does the streaming session need for the Kafka source, and what is the alternative?","a":"<p>It needs the Kafka jars. The commented-out alternative is <code>spark.jars.packages</code> with <code>org.apache.spark:spark-sql-kafka-0-10_2.12:3.5.1</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0089","card":"q-apache-spark-021-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How does Spark read the visits topic as a stream?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>raw_visits_df = streaming_spark\\\n    .readStream\\\n    .format(&quot;kafka&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;kafka.bootstrap.servers&quot;,&quot;localhost:9092&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;subscribe&quot;,&quot;spark.streaming.website.visits&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;startingOffsets&quot;,&quot;latest&quot;)\\\n    .load()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0090","card":"q-apache-spark-021-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How do you turn the Kafka value bytes into columns in Spark?","a":"<p>Cast to string, parse the JSON with the schema, then flatten.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>visits_df = raw_visits_df\\\n    .selectExpr(&quot;CAST(value AS STRING) as value&quot;)\\\n    .select(functions.from_json(&quot;value&quot;, schema).alias(&quot;visits&quot;))\\\n    .select(&quot;visits.*&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0091","card":"q-apache-spark-022-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How does streaming task 1 send abandoned shopping carts to Kafka?","a":"<p>Filter <code>ShoppingCart</code> rows, format them as a value, and write to the <code>spark.streaming.carts.abandoned</code> topic with a checkpoint location.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>shopping_cart_df = visits_df\\\n    .filter(&quot;last_action == &#x27;ShoppingCart&#x27;&quot;)\n    .option(&quot;checkpointLocation&quot;, &quot;tmp/cp-shoppingcart2&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;topic&quot;, &quot;spark.streaming.carts.abandoned&quot;)\\</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0092","card":"q-apache-spark-022-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How does streaming task 2 push country-wise visit duration to Redis?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>visits_df.select(&quot;country&quot;,&quot;duration&quot;)\\\n    .writeStream\\\n    .foreach(write_to_redis)\\\n    .start()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0093","card":"q-apache-spark-022-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How does streaming task 3 compute the sum of duration per last action every 5 seconds?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>windowed_summary = visits_df\\\n    .withColumn(&quot;timestamp&quot;, functions.current_timestamp())\\\n    .withWatermark(&quot;timestamp&quot;,&quot;5 seconds&quot;)\\\n    .groupBy(functions.window(\n            functions.col(&quot;timestamp&quot;),&quot;5 seconds&quot;),\n            functions.col(&quot;last_action&quot;))\\\n    .agg(functions.sum(functions.col(&quot;duration&quot;)).alias(&quot;duration&quot;))</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0094","card":"q-apache-spark-022-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"Which streaming query blocks the notebook, and why do three <code>.start()</code> calls exist?","a":"<p>Each <code>.start()</code> is a separate streaming query. Only the last one blocks with <code>awaitTermination()</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0095","card":"q-apache-spark-022-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"Why must Kafka value bytes be cast and parsed with <code>from_json</code>?","a":"<p>The Kafka <code>value</code> arrives as bytes, so cast it and parse it with <code>from_json</code> plus an explicit schema.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0096","card":"q-apache-spark-022-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"What does the Kafka sink need, and what does <code>foreach</code> do in the streaming job?","a":"<p>The Kafka sink needs <code>checkpointLocation</code>. <code>foreach</code> runs the Python writer per row.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0097","card":"q-apache-spark-022-5-2-streaming-analytics-job-code-04-04","sec":"apache-spark-s018","q":"How is windowing done in Spark Structured Streaming?","a":"<p>Use <code>window()</code> + <code>withWatermark()</code>, then <code>groupBy</code> and aggregate.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0098","card":"q-apache-spark-023-5-3-execute-and-monitor-code-04-05","sec":"apache-spark-s019","q":"How does the monitor notebook read the abandoned-carts Kafka topic?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>visits_topic = &quot;spark.streaming.carts.abandoned&quot;\nvisits_consumer = KafkaConsumer(\n    bootstrap_servers=[&quot;localhost:9092&quot;],\n    group_id=None,\n    value_deserializer=string_deserializer,\n    auto_offset_reset=&quot;latest&quot;\n)\nvisits_consumer.subscribe(visits_topic)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0099","card":"q-apache-spark-023-5-3-execute-and-monitor-code-04-05","sec":"apache-spark-s019","q":"How do you read country totals from the Redis sorted set, highest first?","a":"<p>Use <code>zrevrangebyscore</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>scores = redis_conn.zrevrangebyscore(&quot;last-action-stats&quot;, 99999, 0, withscores=True)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0100","card":"q-apache-spark-023-5-3-execute-and-monitor-code-04-05","sec":"apache-spark-s019","q":"Which MariaDB query does the monitor run for last action stats?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_stats_sql = f&quot;&quot;&quot;\n    SELECT last_action, SUM(duration) as duration\n    FROM `website_stats`.`visit_stats`\n    GROUP BY last_action\n&quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0101","card":"q-apache-spark-023-5-3-execute-and-monitor-code-04-05","sec":"apache-spark-s019","q":"In what order do you run the three real-time notebooks?","a":"<ol>\n  <li><code>code_04_05</code> monitor first.</li>\n  <li><code>code_04_04</code> analytics job.</li>\n  <li><code>code_04_03</code> stream generator.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0102","card":"q-apache-spark-023-5-3-execute-and-monitor-code-04-05","sec":"apache-spark-s019","q":"What do you expect to see when the real-time pipeline runs?","a":"<p>The abandoned-carts topic receives only ShoppingCart records, Redis country totals climb, and MariaDB last-action sums grow per 5-second window.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0103","card":"q-apache-spark-024-scaling-processing","sec":"apache-spark-s020","q":"What are the Spark best practices for scaling processing?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Filter unwanted data early (less data in memory and between executors).</li>\n  <li>Do reduce operations as late as possible (less shuffling). Do parallel work (map, filter) early.</li>\n  <li>Repartition as needed, since some operations create too many partitions.</li>\n  <li>Cache intermediate results that are reused.</li>\n  <li>Avoid actions that send data to the driver. Collect only at the end.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0104","card":"q-apache-spark-025-building-resiliency","sec":"apache-spark-s021","q":"What failures does Spark handle out of the box?","a":"<p>Failures at task, stage and executor level.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0105","card":"q-apache-spark-025-building-resiliency","sec":"apache-spark-s021","q":"How do you build a resilient Spark pipeline?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Monitor jobs and clusters and set up alerting for unhandled failures.</li>\n  <li>Use checkpoints on persistent stores (HDFS, S3) for streaming jobs so they resume after a restart.</li>\n  <li>Make input/output stores redundant and persistent, and deploy Spark on a cluster so one node failure does not stop the pipeline.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The whole solution must be resilient, not only Spark.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0106","card":"q-apache-spark-026-batch-vs-real-time-choosing","sec":"apache-spark-s022","q":"What are the challenges of real-time processing in Spark?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Unbounded datasets make it hard to size memory and clusters.</li>\n  <li>Windowing and watermarks can cause missed events and wrong aggregations.</li>\n  <li>State must be maintained correctly across the cluster.</li>\n  <li>Reprocessing is not a rerun: checkpoints, state and offsets must be reset.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0107","card":"q-apache-spark-026-batch-vs-real-time-choosing","sec":"apache-spark-s022","q":"When do you choose real-time over batch processing?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Responses or actions are required within seconds.</li>\n  <li>Input is a continuous stream of events.</li>\n  <li>Minimal aggregation (more steps add watermark/state complexity).</li>\n  <li>Compute resources are sufficient.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0108","card":"q-apache-spark-026-batch-vs-real-time-choosing","sec":"apache-spark-s022","q":"When do you choose batch over real-time processing?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>A latency of minutes or hours is acceptable.</li>\n  <li>Heavy aggregation and analytics.</li>\n  <li>It is simpler to implement, debug and reprocess.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0109","card":"q-apache-spark-026-batch-vs-real-time-choosing","sec":"apache-spark-s022","q":"What is a hybrid pipeline, and when should you use real-time?","a":"<p>A pipeline that is part batch and part real-time. Use real-time only when the use case demands it.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0110","card":"q-apache-spark-027-scaling-extraction-and-loading","sec":"apache-spark-s023","q":"Why do extraction and loading need attention when scaling a Spark pipeline?","a":"<p>All stages must scale, and extraction/loading (disk reads/writes) are common bottlenecks.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0111","card":"q-apache-spark-027-scaling-extraction-and-loading","sec":"apache-spark-s023","q":"How do you scale extraction in Spark?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Read in parallel (JDBC across executors, Kafka partitions divided between executors).</li>\n  <li>Use each source's parallel-read options. Design source schemas for parallelism.</li>\n  <li>Use predicate pushdown.</li>\n  <li>Defend against missed and duplicate records.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0112","card":"q-apache-spark-027-scaling-extraction-and-loading","sec":"apache-spark-s023","q":"How do you scale loading in Spark?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Each executor writes independently to the sink.</li>\n  <li>Understand sink behavior for transactions, locking and serialization.</li>\n  <li>Cap parallel connections to the sink's capacity.</li>\n  <li>Repartition to control write parallelism.</li>\n  <li>Defend against missed and duplicate updates.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0113","card":"q-apache-spark-028-7-hybrid-pipeline-exercise","sec":"apache-spark-s024","q":"What are the requirements of the Spark hybrid pipeline exercise?","a":"<p>Using the <code>visit_stats</code> table from the real-time website analytics pipeline, build a downstream pipeline for significant actions:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li>A daily job extracts last-action records with duration &gt; 15 (within a 5-second window).</li>\n  <li>Stream them to the Kafka topic <code>spark.exercise.lastaction.long</code> (created in setup).</li>\n  <li>In real time, keep a running counter of significant last actions by action name.</li>\n</ol>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0114","card":"q-apache-spark-028-7-hybrid-pipeline-exercise","sec":"apache-spark-s024","q":"What is the design of the Spark hybrid pipeline exercise?","a":"<p>MariaDB <code>visit_stats</code> -&gt; Job 1 (batch extraction, filter duration &gt; 15, publish to Kafka) -&gt; Kafka topic -&gt; Job 2 (streaming scorecard) -&gt; Redis sorted set of running counts. Batch plus real-time makes it a hybrid pipeline.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0115","card":"q-apache-spark-029-7-1-job-1-extract-long-last-actions-batc","sec":"apache-spark-s025","q":"Which assumption does Job 1 of the hybrid exercise make?","a":"<p>It assumes it runs on the same day the DB was populated.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0116","card":"q-apache-spark-029-7-1-job-1-extract-long-last-actions-batc","sec":"apache-spark-s025","q":"How does Job 1 compute its date range?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>start_date=datetime.datetime.today().strftime(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;)\nend_date=(datetime.datetime.today()+datetime.timedelta(1)).strftime(&quot;%Y-%m-%d&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0117","card":"q-apache-spark-029-7-1-job-1-extract-long-last-actions-batc","sec":"apache-spark-s025","q":"How does Job 1 get the min and max ID bounds for the parallel JDBC read?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>summary_cursor.execute(f&quot;&quot;&quot;\n        SELECT min(`ID`) as MIN_ID, max(`ID`) as MAX_ID\n        FROM `website_stats`.`visit_stats`\n        WHERE `INTERVAL_TIMESTAMP` BETWEEN\n            &#x27;{start_date}&#x27; AND &#x27;{end_date}&#x27;\n    &quot;&quot;&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0118","card":"q-apache-spark-029-7-1-job-1-extract-long-last-actions-batc","sec":"apache-spark-s025","q":"Which query selects the long last actions in Job 1?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>last_action_query= f&quot;&quot;&quot;\n            SELECT ID, LAST_ACTION, DURATION\n            FROM `website_stats`.`visit_stats`\n             WHERE `INTERVAL_TIMESTAMP` BETWEEN\n                &#x27;{start_date}&#x27; AND &#x27;{end_date}&#x27;\n            AND DURATION &gt; 15\n        &quot;&quot;&quot;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0119","card":"q-apache-spark-030-7-1-job-1-extract-long-last-actions-batc","sec":"apache-spark-s025","q":"How does Job 1 name its Spark session?","a":"<p>The session is the same as <code>streaming_spark</code> but with <code>appName(\"LongLastActionsJob\")</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>website_spark = SparkSession\\\n            .builder\\\n            .appName(&quot;LongLastActionsJob&quot;)\\</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0120","card":"q-apache-spark-030-7-1-job-1-extract-long-last-actions-batc","sec":"apache-spark-s025","q":"How does Job 1 read the long last actions from MariaDB in parallel?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>last_action_df = website_spark.read\\\n            .format(&quot;jdbc&quot;)\\\n            .option(&quot;url&quot;, &quot;jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/website_stats&quot;)\\\n            .option(&quot;dbtable&quot;, &quot;( &quot; + last_action_query + &quot; ) as tmpLastAction&quot;)\\\n            .option(&quot;user&quot;, &quot;spark&quot;)\\\n            .option(&quot;password&quot;, &quot;spark&quot;)\\\n            .option(&quot;partitionColumn&quot;,&quot;ID&quot;)\\\n            .option(&quot;lowerBound&quot;, min_bounds)\\\n            .option(&quot;upperBound&quot;,max_bounds + 1)\\\n            .option(&quot;numPartitions&quot;,2)\\\n            .load()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0121","card":"q-apache-spark-030-7-1-job-1-extract-long-last-actions-batc","sec":"apache-spark-s025","q":"How does Job 1 publish the long last actions to Kafka?","a":"<p>It does a batch write with <code>LAST_ACTION</code> as both key and value.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>last_action_df.selectExpr(&quot;LAST_ACTION as key&quot;, &quot;LAST_ACTION as value&quot;)\\\n        .write\\\n        .format(&quot;kafka&quot;)\\\n        .option(&quot;checkpointLocation&quot;, &quot;/tmp/cp-lastaction&quot;)\\\n        .option(&quot;kafka.bootstrap.servers&quot;, &quot;localhost:9092&quot;)\\\n        .option(&quot;topic&quot;, &quot;spark.exercise.lastaction.long&quot;)\\\n        .save();</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0122","card":"q-apache-spark-031-7-2-job-2-scorecard-streaming-code-06-04","sec":"apache-spark-s026","q":"How does Job 2 of the hybrid exercise count each long last action in Redis?","a":"<p>It increments the action's score by 1 in the sorted set <code>long-last-action-stats</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>stats_key=&quot;long-last-action-stats&quot;\nredis_conn.zincrby(stats_key, 1, row[&quot;last_action&quot;])</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0123","card":"q-apache-spark-031-7-2-job-2-scorecard-streaming-code-06-04","sec":"apache-spark-s026","q":"How does Job 2 read the Kafka topic, and how does it differ from the website visits streaming job?","a":"<p>It reads with <code>startingOffsets</code> set to <code>earliest</code>, which consumes the topic from the beginning. the website visits streaming job used <code>latest</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>    .option(&quot;subscribe&quot;,&quot;spark.exercise.lastaction.long&quot;)\\\n    .option(&quot;startingOffsets&quot;,&quot;earliest&quot;)\\</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0124","card":"q-apache-spark-031-7-2-job-2-scorecard-streaming-code-06-04","sec":"apache-spark-s026","q":"Why does Job 2 need no schema?","a":"<p>There is only one value field, so it casts the value directly to string.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>last_action_df = raw_last_action_df\\\n                .selectExpr(&quot;CAST(value as STRING) as last_action&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0125","card":"q-apache-spark-031-7-2-job-2-scorecard-streaming-code-06-04","sec":"apache-spark-s026","q":"How does Job 2 write the stream to Redis?","a":"<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>last_action_df.select(&quot;last_action&quot;)\\\n        .writeStream\\\n        .foreach(write_to_redis)\\\n        .start()</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0126","card":"q-apache-spark-031-7-2-job-2-scorecard-streaming-code-06-04","sec":"apache-spark-s026","q":"How does Job 2 watch the running counts?","a":"<p>It polls the sorted set every 5 seconds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>scores=redis_query_conn.zrevrangebyscore(\n    &quot;long-last-action-stats&quot;,99999,0,withscores=True)\ntime.sleep(5)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0127","card":"q-apache-spark-031-7-2-job-2-scorecard-streaming-code-06-04","sec":"apache-spark-s026","q":"What are the key techniques of the Spark hybrid pipeline exercise?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Parallel JDBC read via <code>partitionColumn</code>, <code>lowerBound</code>, <code>upperBound</code>, <code>numPartitions</code>, with the filter query wrapped as a subquery in <code>dbtable</code>.</li>\n  <li>The same Kafka topic is written by a batch job (<code>write</code>) and read by a streaming job (<code>readStream</code>).</li>\n  <li><code>zincrby</code> on a Redis sorted set increments counts atomically.</li>\n  <li><code>startingOffsets: earliest</code> consumes the topic from the beginning. the website visits streaming job used <code>latest</code>.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"apache-spark-f0128","card":"q-apache-spark-032-8-next-steps","sec":"apache-spark-s027","q":"What are the suggested next steps after the Spark data engineering course?","a":"<p>Explore more batch and stream use cases with Spark, study comparable tools (Kafka Streams, Apache Flink), and apply the techniques to a real data engineering problem.</p>","hand":true}];
